{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Two cherubim.</b> A form of a bird, as it is written in Ezekiel: ״את כרוב ממשח הסוכך״ — he explained: a great bird with wings. Even though it said, 'You shall not make for yourself a carved image or any likeness,' here the form of the cherubim was permitted, for they were not made to be worshipped, but for His seat, in the manner of the cherubim of the Throne of Glory. And many such cases we find in the Torah, as written: 'all who do work on it shall die' — yet work was permitted on it for the regular offering, the additional offering, circumcision, the forbidden relations of a brother's wife and levirate marriage, 'you shall not wear sha'atnez,' 'you shall make for yourself fringes.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:23.537305443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}